{"uid":"5679769ce260e8b8","name":"test_three_uncorroborated_no_verdict_claims_now_back_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","fullName":"tests.test_uncorroborated_claim_three_strike_task006#test_three_uncorroborated_no_verdict_claims_now_back_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","historyId":"19c9b2e9160006d347a52fd72ce29e8a","time":{"start":1791959961017,"stop":1791959961615,"duration":598},"description":"Repeated worker iterations on the one seeded task, each claiming\n    `commit` progress evidence with no real workspace delta behind it --\n    uncorroborated every time -- driven through the REAL production\n    pipeline (`_run_job_core()`, `max_approaches=1`, the default\n    `vigilant=True` last-approach behaviour) rather than a raw\n    `_step_worker()` call.\n\n    This test used to prove requirement B.4's own words: that removing the\n    legacy absorption dispatch (task 004) \"must not remove\" the ordinary\n    three-strike stagnation witness for a claim that fails corroboration,\n    landing the run at `paused`/`stagnation`. PRD v0.29 #279 (task 014's\n    sweep cure, same reasoning as `tests/test_progress_budget_task013.py`'s\n    and `tests/test_progress_pin_task015.py`'s own sibling rewrites)\n    supersedes that for this exact shape: `_apply_engine_repoll_backoff`'s\n    trigger is the SAME signal (`no_verdict`, `corroborated: false`,\n    `deltaSize: 0`, two consecutive times on one task) this scenario\n    scripts on every single pass, so from the second claim onward every\n    further claim is ALSO the second-or-later of a still-running re-poll\n    streak -- it backs off (doubling each time, capped at 1800s) rather\n    than ever feeding the three-strike counter a second or third witness,\n    for as long as the task keeps re-polling identically. With the\n    harness's `asyncio.sleep` patched instant (`make_supervisor`'s\n    default), the run spins through its own 20-iteration budget\n    (`_spw010_supervisor`'s own `iterations=20`) in increasingly\n    backed-off re-polls and ends `exhausted` (budget exhausted, task never\n    completed, never paused) rather than ever reaching the old\n    `paused`/`stagnation` outcome\n    `tests/test_worker_hat.py::test_a_plan_with_work_left_is_never_\n    routed_to_review` still pins for the pre-#279, non-repoll-shaped\n    guard.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Repeated worker iterations on the one seeded task, each claiming<br />\n<code>commit</code> progress evidence with no real workspace delta behind it --<br />\nuncorroborated every time -- driven through the REAL production<br />\npipeline (<code>_run_job_core()</code>, <code>max_approaches=1</code>, the default<br />\n<code>vigilant=True</code> last-approach behaviour) rather than a raw<br />\n<code>_step_worker()</code> call.</p>\n<pre><code>This test used to prove requirement B.4's own words: that removing the\nlegacy absorption dispatch (task 004) &quot;must not remove&quot; the ordinary\nthree-strike stagnation witness for a claim that fails corroboration,\nlanding the run at `paused`/`stagnation`. PRD v0.29 #279 (task 014's\nsweep cure, same reasoning as `tests/test_progress_budget_task013.py`'s\nand `tests/test_progress_pin_task015.py`'s own sibling rewrites)\nsupersedes that for this exact shape: `_apply_engine_repoll_backoff`'s\ntrigger is the SAME signal (`no_verdict`, `corroborated: false`,\n`deltaSize: 0`, two consecutive times on one task) this scenario\nscripts on every single pass, so from the second claim onward every\nfurther claim is ALSO the second-or-later of a still-running re-poll\nstreak -- it backs off (doubling each time, capped at 1800s) rather\nthan ever feeding the three-strike counter a second or third witness,\nfor as long as the task keeps re-polling identically. With the\nharness's `asyncio.sleep` patched instant (`make_supervisor`'s\ndefault), the run spins through its own 20-iteration budget\n(`_spw010_supervisor`'s own `iterations=20`) in increasingly\nbacked-off re-polls and ends `exhausted` (budget exhausted, task never\ncompleted, never paused) rather than ever reaching the old\n`paused`/`stagnation` outcome\n`tests/test_worker_hat.py::test_a_plan_with_work_left_is_never_\nrouted_to_review` still pins for the pre-#279, non-repoll-shaped\nguard.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791959389106,"stop":1791959389106,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791959389106,"stop":1791959389106,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791959960967,"stop":1791959960981,"duration":14},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791959960967,"stop":1791959960967,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791959960981,"stop":1791959960982,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791959960982,"stop":1791959961000,"duration":18},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount